's silence\nreadable and its known stops self-describing.\n\n## Head\n\n`dc98bcfe60a5dab0b5a18a4a57a5561b9a4a89a2` merges main `cb7cb25` into the previous head: an automatic merge by the orchestrator, no resolution. The reviewed code is unchanged.\n\nbd8bf3d325d8d83eba43141ce5b0b7959da228b1\n\n## Mutation proof\n\n`python3 tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py --self-test` (in tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py) — each mutant below was applied to the working tree and re-run:\n\n- beat advance shifted off the boundary (`due = now + HEARTBEAT_SECONDS + 1`), recarry START line and overlap start line replaced by `pass`: 4 red — the two beat arms, the recarry-START arm, the overlap start arm.\n- beat line text renamed (`beat:` → `BEAT-MUTANT`), `cls=HOLDER` dropped, carry's ancestor-shape detection short-circuited (`if True:`): 4 red — both beat arms, the HOLDER arm, the STALE-VERDICT-CARRY arm.\n- `cls=ROW_MISSING` dropped: 1 red — the ROW-MISSING arm.\n\n## Null control\n\nThe unmodified tree (main's merge_train) passes the same suite minus the new\narms; every pre-existing arm is unchanged and green — no beat line can appear\nin an old expectation, because a wait that settles inside HEARTBEAT_SECONDS\nprints nothing (`beat:` appears in zero lines of the null-control arm, asserted\nexplicitly), and every stop line without a known class keeps today's exact\n`TRAIN STOPPED <step>:` / `SKIP #<pr> <phase>:` prefix.\n\n## Figures\n\n- `python3 tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py --self-test` → `merge_train self-test: 119 checks, 0 failed`\n- `HEARTBEAT_SECONDS = 240` (constant in tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py); the beat is time-based against the poll clock, so a poll cadence slower or faster than 240s still beats on time — asserted at t+240/t+480/t+960 on a stubbed clock that jumps 100/240/300/480/700/960.\n\n## Red checks\n\n`closures-autofix` — red once at branch commit bd8bf3d32 (06:19Z) on an\nartifact-expiry infra failure (\"Artifact not found for name:\nclosure-recordings\"), not a code defect: there was nothing for the lane to\nrepair, and its run at the head is `skipped`. The cheaper detector is the\nlane itself — it re-fires on every push and would name a real closure\ndefect; its standing cost is one check-run per push. No other red: `tools/audit/`\nis INERT in tests/closures.json, so this diff scopes to zero gate scripts\n(the branch's own gate prints `MODE: SCOPED -- 0 script(s) run`; key on the\nmode line, not the zero).\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone\n\n## Friction\n\nnone\n\n\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T17:57:13Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T17:57:11Z","merged_at":"2026-10-13T17:57:11Z","merge_commit_sha":"c7a70cb24ff8eaaaf4cb588c05c842ce8b225dec","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2169/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2169/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2169/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/dc98bcfe60a5dab0b5a18a4a57a5561b9a4a89a2","head":{"label":"tvofi:feat/train-heartbeat","ref":"feat/train-heartbeat","sha":"dc98bcfe60a5dab0b5a18a4a57a5561b9a4a89a2","user":{"login":"tvofi","id":70032254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMDMyMjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.g